,"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":538,"wikidataSitelinks":8,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["sirjohnguisestadium","portmoresby"],"summary":"The Sir John Guise Stadium is a multi-sport and athletics venue located in Port Moresby, the capital city of Papua New Guinea, and is part of the larger Sir John Guise Sports Precinct which also includes an indoor arena, beach volleyball/hockey court, and aquatics center.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Sir John Guise Stadium","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fd/Sir._John_Guise_Stadium.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fd/Sir._John_Guise_Stadium.jpg","w":1200,"h":789,"author":"derivative work: Rhinen","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir._John_Guise_Stadium.jpg"}},{"id":"port_moresby_sir_hubert_murray_stadium","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Sir Hubert Murray Stadium","category":"other","tags":["family"],"location":{"lat":-9.46694,"lng":147.15667},"visitMinutes":90,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_sir_hubert_murray_stadium","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":1,"wikiPageviews":223,"wikidataSitelinks":9,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["sirhubertmurraystadium","portmoresby"],"summary":"The Hubert Murray Stadium is a sports venue located in Port Moresby, the capital city of Papua New Guinea. It was developed for the 1969 South Pacific Games on reclaimed land at Konedobu that had previously been shoreline mangroves.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Sir Hubert Murray Stadium","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Sir_Hubert_Murray_Stadium_%281993%2C_cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Sir_Hubert_Murray_Stadium_%281993%2C_cropped%29.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Sir_Hubert_Murray_Stadium_%281993%2C_cropped%29.jpg/500px-Sir_Hubert_Murray_Stadium_%281993%2C_cropped%29.jpg","w":1200,"h":664,"author":"lindsaybridge","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Hubert_Murray_Stadium_(1993,_cropped).jpg"}},{"id":"port_moresby_wv_national_parliament_of_papua_new_guinea","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"National Parliament of Papua New Guinea","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":-9.42806,"lng":147.19191},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_wv_national_parliament_of_papua_new_guinea","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["nationalparliamentofpapuanewguinea","portmoresby"],"summary":"Parliament Haus is one of the most impressive buildings in Port Moresby, built in the style of a Maprik Haus Tambaran (house of spirits from East Sepik Province). Dating from 1984, it is usually open to visitors.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Port Moresby"},{"id":"port_moresby_wv_touaguba_hill","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Touaguba Hill","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":-9.47478,"lng":147.15983},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_wv_touaguba_hill","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["touagubahill","portmoresby"],"summary":"Perhaps not so much to see, but this is where the ambassadorial residences are located and is also where many of the well-to-do expats and locals live. There is a nice view from the top of the hill overlooking the centre of the city and the ocean.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Port Moresby"},{"id":"port_moresby_wv_port_moresby_golf_club","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Port Moresby Golf Club","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":-9.42357,"lng":147.1917},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_wv_port_moresby_golf_club","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["portmoresbygolfclub","portmoresby"],"summary":"A nice golf course located right across from the government buildings. The prices are quite acceptable for visitors. Be careful: crocodiles inhabit the water holes of the golf course. The main building has a nice restaurant where one can have lunch and have a few SP beers (South Pacific beers) after a round of golf.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Port Moresby"},{"id":"port_moresby_wv_ela_beach_craft_market","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Ela Beach Craft Market","category":"beach","tags":["beach","sea","nature","sunset"],"location":{"lat":-9.48112,"lng":147.15175},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_wv_ela_beach_craft_market","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["elabeachcraftmarket","portmoresby"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Run by the Ela Murray International School and held on the last Saturday of each month, this market brings together local artifacts from all over Papua New Guinea. An easy way to get some beautiful carvings, handwoven baskets, or any of a number of other things to bring home as souvenirs.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Port Moresby"}],"sources":["Wikidata (CC0)","Wikimedia Commons (counts; photos credited per file)","Wikipedia (pageviews; summaries CC BY-SA 4.0)","Wikivoyage (listings: hours, prices, descriptions; CC BY-SA 4.0)","OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL): opening hours, fees, websites"]}